  "removedFiles": [],
  "changes": [
    "Exact author v1.1.67 release, original version/attribution/MIT license retained; explicitly community-maintained adaptation for 0.2.1-alpha.1.",
    "Mandatory absolute launcher profileContext/DSH_HOME; no default home, global host scanning or boot-time shared-core patching.",
    "Explicit Apply backs up and patches current-host physical private copies, then selects current-profile bundle aliases with original IDs/configuration/expressions. Failed patches roll back before mounting.",
    "Revert restores owned private core and alias/dependency/name fields while preserving later user configuration. Crash partial state fails closed and has a standalone explicit-home/profile recovery CLI.",
    "Native write and backup guards reject links/junctions/other profiles/shared core; exclusive random temporary files, atomic replacement and filesystem sync for supported managed writes.",
    "Actual community client UI injection, native Context/Loader/profile resolver, current-host RedTeam tools dependency resolution and cold module imports adapted.",
    "Current DSH_HOME prompt/rules/skills/net scope/drill settings remain functional with managed path guards and custom prompt preservation.",
    "RedTeam startup uses missing-only preset/skill/setup/anchor assets; automatic SQLite migration only adds schema and missing defaults, preserving legacy stages/columns/points/hits and existing field values.",
    "Official ASAR/global CLI/deny-hook mutation/self-update/self-uninstall/automatic restart primitives and HTTP routes reject in this adaptation; plugin manager handles update/uninstall and full restart is manual."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Apply and Revert affect only private copies owned by the current profile and require manually quitting and restarting that DSH client.",
    "Official ASAR, global CLI, native self-update, self-uninstall and automatic restart are disabled; update/uninstall use the community plugin manager. Revert the private overlay before uninstall.",
    "Prompt, rules and skills retain the current DSH_HOME paths, which can be shared by profiles using the same home. Existing customized prompt content is preserved on startup.",
    "Full Electron desktop, model API, every preset and session rewind workflow have not been executed end to end; no author endorsement or universal compatibility claim.",
    "Optional native hooks that modify host-wide deny rules are disabled. Actual web composition matched 34 patches and 11 existing matches; 30 optional or layout-specific patches were unmatched and are reported.",
    "Existing RedTeam presets, skills and setup script are preserved on startup; existing database rows and legacy columns are not removed or automatically rewritten."
  ],
